1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,902
For more than a decade,

2
00:00:02,922 --> 00:00:07,487
scientists believed there was a wall
around Earth that nothing could cross.

3
00:00:07,667 --> 00:00:13,121
Not a wall of stone, or metal. A wall made
of magnetism and invisible waves,

4
00:00:13,141 --> 00:00:16,790
floating thousands of kilometers above
your head.

5
00:00:16,970 --> 00:00:19,437
They called it the impenetrable barrier.

6
00:00:19,617 --> 00:00:24,238
And in May 2024, the Sun threw everything
it had at it.

7
00:00:24,418 --> 00:00:27,806
What happened next was recorded by a
Japanese satellite,

8
00:00:27,826 --> 00:00:29,893
and it has just been published.

9
00:00:30,073 --> 00:00:32,607
Deadly, near light speed electrons
appeared

10
00:00:32,627 --> 00:00:35,420
exactly where they were never supposed to
be.

11
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:40,435
Stay with me, because the way they got
there is stranger than anyone expected.

12
00:00:41,215 --> 00:00:45,580
To understand the breach, we first need to
meet the Van Allen belts.

13
00:00:45,760 --> 00:00:47,897
Earth is wrapped in two giant,

14
00:00:47,917 --> 00:00:51,377
donut shaped regions of trapped charged
particles,

15
00:00:51,397 --> 00:00:54,648
held in place by our planet's magnetic
field.

16
00:00:54,828 --> 00:00:57,367
The inner belt is mostly protons,

17
00:00:57,387 --> 00:01:02,110
many of them created when cosmic rays slam
into our atmosphere.

18
00:01:02,130 --> 00:01:05,487
It sits roughly 600 to 6,000 kilometers
up.

19
00:01:05,667 --> 00:01:12,382
The outer belt is mostly electrons,
energized by processes driven by the Sun.

20
00:01:12,402 --> 00:01:18,032
It stretches from about 13,500 kilometers
out to around 60,000.

21
00:01:18,212 --> 00:01:22,428
Between them lies a gap called the slot,
usually almost empty.

22
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:26,336
Some of those electrons are the dangerous
kind.

23
00:01:26,516 --> 00:01:30,684
Scientists call them ultra-relativistic,
or killer electrons,

24
00:01:30,704 --> 00:01:34,807
because they are accelerated to nearly the
speed of light.

25
00:01:34,987 --> 00:01:38,252
Their energy is so high that they can
punch through

26
00:01:38,272 --> 00:01:41,806
satellite shielding and damage sensitive
electronics.

27
00:01:41,986 --> 00:01:45,391
Over time, that can shorten the life of a
spacecraft.

28
00:01:45,571 --> 00:01:48,848
They also raise the radiation risk for
astronauts.

29
00:01:49,028 --> 00:01:52,467
So where these particles can and cannot go
decides

30
00:01:52,487 --> 00:01:56,273
how we design and protect everything we
put in orbit.

31
00:01:57,053 --> 00:02:02,741
Then, in 2014, NASA's twin Van Allen
Probes found something strange.

32
00:02:02,921 --> 00:02:07,290
The most energetic electrons seemed to
stop at a weirdly sharp edge,

33
00:02:07,310 --> 00:02:10,593
about three Earth radii from the planet's
center.

34
00:02:10,773 --> 00:02:14,840
On one side, a swarm of them. On the
other, almost nothing.

35
00:02:15,020 --> 00:02:19,283
The team, led by Daniel Baker, published
it in the journal Nature,

36
00:02:19,303 --> 00:02:22,927
and gave it a dramatic name: the
impenetrable barrier.

37
00:02:23,107 --> 00:02:27,824
Their explanation was that the electrons
drift inward extremely slowly,

38
00:02:27,844 --> 00:02:31,693
while faint waves in the cloud of cold
plasma around Earth

39
00:02:31,713 --> 00:02:35,302
keep scattering them away, down into the
atmosphere.

40
00:02:35,482 --> 00:02:40,295
Together, those effects built what looked
like an invisible glass wall in space.

41
00:02:41,075 --> 00:02:42,500
But almost immediately,

42
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:46,251
other scientists started to doubt that it
was a wall at all.

43
00:02:46,431 --> 00:02:51,266
In 2018, a team proposed that the barrier
might be an illusion.

44
00:02:51,446 --> 00:02:54,693
Storms that push electrons inward, they
argued,

45
00:02:54,713 --> 00:02:58,446
usually die out before the electrons get
much farther.

46
00:02:58,466 --> 00:03:02,617
So the edge may only be where the storms
run out of steam.

47
00:03:02,797 --> 00:03:04,619
Then came another hint.

48
00:03:04,639 --> 00:03:10,683
Researchers digging through observations
from 1996 to 2006 found that lightning

49
00:03:10,703 --> 00:03:16,272
generated radio waves can knock killer
electrons out of the inner belt.

50
00:03:16,452 --> 00:03:19,237
Which meant energetic electrons were
already

51
00:03:19,257 --> 00:03:21,735
living inside the supposed boundary.

52
00:03:21,915 --> 00:03:26,740
Records from the huge Halloween storms of
2003 even suggested that

53
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:32,019
extreme storms had once pushed energetic
electrons deep into the slot.

54
00:03:32,199 --> 00:03:38,207
But nobody had watched it happen with a
modern satellite. Until May 2024.

55
00:03:38,987 --> 00:03:45,074
May 2024. The Sun erupts in a series of
flares and coronal mass ejections,

56
00:03:45,094 --> 00:03:50,990
hurling billions of tons of magnetized
plasma across the solar system.

57
00:03:51,170 --> 00:03:56,361
A day or so later, the wave front slams
into Earth's magnetic field,

58
00:03:56,381 --> 00:04:00,653
and our planet experiences a level G5
geomagnetic storm.

59
00:04:00,673 --> 00:04:03,322
The strongest category there is.

60
00:04:03,502 --> 00:04:06,952
It was the most powerful storm in about
two decades.

61
00:04:06,972 --> 00:04:10,289
Auroras danced as far south as Florida and
Mexico,

62
00:04:10,309 --> 00:04:14,566
and its effects were even recorded at the
bottom of the ocean.

63
00:04:14,746 --> 00:04:18,660
Up in space, the storm squeezed Earth's
magnetic bubble,

64
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:22,875
and crushed the plasmasphere, that
protective cloud of cold,

65
00:04:22,895 --> 00:04:25,895
dense plasma, harder than ever recorded.

66
00:04:26,075 --> 00:04:31,294
At the same time, the outer belt lost a
huge share of its energetic electrons.

67
00:04:31,474 --> 00:04:36,885
And in the middle of all this chaos, one
Japanese spacecraft was working perfectly.

68
00:04:37,665 --> 00:04:42,516
That spacecraft is Arase, launched by
Japan's space agency,

69
00:04:42,536 --> 00:04:47,940
JAXA, and it has been monitoring the
radiation belts since 2017.

70
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:53,627
A team led by Yoshizumi Miyoshi at Nagoya
University went through its data,

71
00:04:53,647 --> 00:04:56,347
and saw something nobody expected.

72
00:04:56,527 --> 00:05:02,204
Normally, that dense cloud of cold plasma
damps out certain electromagnetic waves,

73
00:05:02,224 --> 00:05:04,498
like a blanket over a speaker.

74
00:05:04,678 --> 00:05:09,175
But the storm had stripped away much of
the cloud. With the blanket gone,

75
00:05:09,195 --> 00:05:13,523
a different kind of wave could thrive.
They are called chorus waves.

76
00:05:13,703 --> 00:05:16,091
Convert them to audio, says Miyoshi,

77
00:05:16,111 --> 00:05:20,202
and they sound like birdsong. Rising
chirps, again and again.

78
00:05:20,382 --> 00:05:26,066
And in this thin, empty environment, those
waves did not scatter the electrons away.

79
00:05:26,086 --> 00:05:29,936
They did the opposite. They pushed them,
again and again,

80
00:05:29,956 --> 00:05:34,625
to enormous energies, right where the
barrier was supposed to hold.

81
00:05:35,405 --> 00:05:37,402
Here is what Arase measured.

82
00:05:37,582 --> 00:05:42,502
During the recovery phase of the storm,
electrons inside the barrier surged.

83
00:05:42,682 --> 00:05:45,904
At energies around 3 million electron
volts,

84
00:05:45,924 --> 00:05:51,570
the flux ballooned by more than 5,000
times compared with before the storm.

85
00:05:51,750 --> 00:05:56,833
And the timing tells the story. Lower
energy electrons showed up first.

86
00:05:56,853 --> 00:05:59,995
About half a day later came higher
energies.

87
00:06:00,015 --> 00:06:03,086
And roughly a day after the first
increase,

88
00:06:03,106 --> 00:06:07,251
electrons above 3 million electron volts
had surged too.

89
00:06:07,431 --> 00:06:11,214
That staggered climb is the fingerprint of
acceleration.

90
00:06:11,234 --> 00:06:16,788
These electrons were not swept in from
outside. They were energized on the spot.

91
00:06:16,968 --> 00:06:22,138
The data also showed a distinct peak in
the electron distribution right near

92
00:06:22,158 --> 00:06:27,605
the old boundary, a pattern that is hard
to explain by inward transport alone.

93
00:06:27,785 --> 00:06:32,257
The wall was not broken from the outside.
It was breached from within.

94
00:06:33,037 --> 00:06:38,145
The extra radiation did not vanish
quickly. It lingered for months,

95
00:06:38,165 --> 00:06:44,101
and Arase watched it fade until another
solar storm arrived in October 2024.

96
00:06:44,281 --> 00:06:49,706
Separately, a small NASA CubeSat called
CIRBE found that the same superstorm

97
00:06:49,726 --> 00:06:54,219
carved two temporary new belts into the
slot. One held protons,

98
00:06:54,239 --> 00:06:57,798
something never seen before in a temporary
belt.

99
00:06:57,978 --> 00:07:01,195
Is any of this a danger to people on the
ground?

100
00:07:01,215 --> 00:07:04,775
No. The belts sit thousands of kilometers
above us.

101
00:07:04,955 --> 00:07:08,458
But for satellites and astronauts, it is a
big deal.

102
00:07:08,478 --> 00:07:11,646
It shows that a safe zone is not always
safe.

103
00:07:11,826 --> 00:07:17,214
Miyoshi says we need to understand how
energetic electrons behave under extreme

104
00:07:17,234 --> 00:07:22,762
space weather, to judge the radiation risk
to spacecraft and improve forecasts.

105
00:07:23,542 --> 00:07:26,179
So was the impenetrable barrier a myth?

106
00:07:26,359 --> 00:07:29,430
Not exactly. Under normal conditions, it
holds.

107
00:07:29,450 --> 00:07:32,850
But Earth's shield turns out to be less
like a wall,

108
00:07:32,870 --> 00:07:38,383
and more like a living system, one that
can change character in a matter of hours.

109
00:07:38,563 --> 00:07:42,408
The Sun's activity rises and falls on an
eleven year cycle,

110
00:07:42,428 --> 00:07:47,003
and every big storm is a new experiment
for the satellites watching.

111
00:07:47,183 --> 00:07:51,631
If you enjoyed this journey into the
invisible space above our heads,

112
00:07:51,651 --> 00:07:56,714
hit subscribe, and tell me in the
comments: what should we explore next?
